    "id": "gh-234-time-blocking-mastery-calendar-control",
    "title": "Time Blocking Mastery: Taking Control of Your Calendar",
    "slug": "time-blocking-mastery-calendar-control",
    "category": "Professional Development",
    "excerpt": "Reactive calendars lead to reactive careers. Learn time blocking to proactively design your days, protect focus time, and achieve important goals.",
    "content": "# Time Blocking Mastery: Taking Control of Your Calendar\n\nYour calendar controls your life. If you don't control your calendar, others will.\n\nTime blocking is proactive calendar management: scheduling specific time blocks for specific work.\n\nInstead of reacting to requests, you design your ideal week.\n\n## What Is Time Blocking?\n\n**Scheduling your entire day in blocks:**\n\n- 9-11 AM: Deep work on Project X\n- 11-12 PM: Email and Slack\n- 12-1 PM: Lunch\n- 1-2:30 PM: Meetings\n- 2:30-4 PM: Deep work on Project Y\n- 4-5 PM: Planning and admin\n\n**Every hour has purpose.**\n\n## Benefits of Time Blocking\n\n**Proactive vs reactive:**\nYou decide priorities, not your inbox.\n\n**Protected focus time:**\nDeep work blocks are sacred.\n\n**Realistic planning:**\nSee what actually fits in day.\n\n**Reduced decision fatigue:**\nKnow what to work on when.\n\n**Better boundaries:**\nClear when you're available vs not.\n\n## How to Time Block\n\n**Step 1: Identify your priorities**\n\nWhat outcomes matter this week?\n\n**Step 2: Estimate time needed**\n\nHow long will priority work take?\n\n**Step 3: Block your calendar**\n\nSchedule blocks for priority work first.\n\nThen meetings, admin, email.\n\n**Step 4: Protect blocks**\n\nTreat time blocks like meetings—non-negotiable.\n\n**Step 5: Review and adjust**\n\nDaily: adjust as needed\nWeekly: improve system\n\n## Types of Time Blocks\n\n**Deep work blocks:**\n90-180 minutes for focused work.\n\nMorning when fresh.\n\n**Meeting blocks:**\nBatch meetings when possible.\n\nExample: Tuesdays and Thursdays 1-5 PM.\n\n**Admin blocks:**\nEmail, Slack, scheduling.\n\n30-60 minutes, 2-3x daily.\n\n**Break blocks:**\nLunch, walks, recovery.\n\nSchedule them. They matter.\n\n**Buffer blocks:**\nUnexpected issues, overflow work.\n\n**Planning blocks:**\nWeekly planning, daily reviews.\n\n## Template Weeks\n\n**Create ideal week template:**\n\nMonday:\n- 9-11: Deep work\n- 11-12: Admin\n- 1-3: Meetings\n- 3-5: Project work\n\nRepeat for each day.\n\nNot rigid—starting point.\n\n## Common Time Blocking Mistakes\n\n**Mistake 1: Over-scheduling**\n\nNo buffer. Cascading delays.\n\n**Fix:** Schedule to 75% capacity.\n\n**Mistake 2: Too rigid**\n\nLife happens. Flexibility needed.\n\n**Fix:** Build in buffer time.\n\n**Mistake 3: Not protecting blocks**\n\nAllowing meetings to overwrite focus time.\n\n**Fix:** Defend your blocks.\n\n**Mistake 4: Unrealistic estimates**\n\nThings take longer than expected.\n\n**Fix:** Add 25% to estimates.\n\n## Tools for Time Blocking\n\n**Digital calendars:**\n- Google Calendar\n- Outlook\n- Apple Calendar\n\n**Time blocking apps:**\n- Reclaim.ai\n- Clockwise\n- SavvyCal\n\n**Paper planners:**\nSome people prefer analog.\n\n## Final Thoughts\n\nTime blocking transforms reactive days into proactive ones.\n\nYou decide what matters. You protect time for it. You make progress on priorities.\n\nStart simple. One week. Adjust. Improve.\n\nYour calendar is your life. Design it intentionally.",
    "seoTitle": "Time Blocking Mastery: Take Control of Your Calendar [2025]",
    "seoDescription": "Master time blocking to proactively design your days, protect focus time, and achieve important goals. Stop reacting, start designing your time.",
    "seoKeywords": [
      "time blocking",
      "calendar management",
      "productivity",
      "time management",
      "focus time",
      "scheduling",
      "proactive planning"
    ],
